carlhnelson@gmail.com wrote:
> My current character is a XL15 orcish barbarian with Int=7 and Wis=11.
> With loot from altar camping and a WoW in Sokoban I have almost all of
> my gear (SDSM,speed boots, cloak of magic resistance, stormy, cleaver,
> silver saber).  What I'm wondering now is whether I should spend any
> significant amount of time trying to learn spells. 

I wouldn't delay a game because of that; if you can ascend go for it.

The only spells that you may enhance to 'skilled' are attack spells.
Other spell classes are restricted for barbarians; you will only be able
to cast the low level spells. And you don't have a lot mana points anyway.

> Should I use a wish
> for a helm of brilliance and risk encounters with mind flayers to raise
> my int? 

No to the latter. If you don't need, say, ESP from a helmet you may as
well wish for a helm of brilliance. But your base Int is low, so you
will also need some blessed potions of gain ability (or the equivalent
positive results from a magic fountain), or some blessed potion of
enlightenment.

> This is my first barbarian (well 11th, but the first 10 don't
> count) and I could use some advice on what to expect for later in the
> game.  So far I can cast Force Bolt with a fail rate of 91%.  I'd like
> to be able to cast create monster and would love to be able to cast
> identify but perhaps those spells are not to be part of this game? 

All spells are part of the game, none is excluded. It's just that some
classes are more other less restricted in spellcasting. For example...

Create monster is a level 2 clerical spell; as a low level spell you
may cast it as a barbarian (with your current stats at 93% failure).

Identify is a level 3 divination spell. As a level 15 barbarian you
need some Int:22 to cast it with 90% failure (wearing a robe makes
that 50%).

> Any
> advice would be appreciated.  

You may like to play around with this spell calculator to see how you
need to enhance your stats and level to cast the spells you like

   http://www.gridbug.de/spells.html

but you need also to have the right spellbooks.

